## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical diagnostic reasoning for common cross-region latency issues, focusing on DNS routing, TLS termination, and edge pathing rather than code changes.

## Key Concepts

- DNS routing and TTL effects
- TLS handshake timing across regions
- Edge NAT/firewall behavior and LB logs
- Basic network measurement tools (dig, curl, mtr, openssl)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: measure DNS and HTTP timings in Node.js
const https = require('https');
const start = Date.now();
https.get('https://api.example.com/ping', res => {
  res.resume();
  res.on('end', () => console.log('elapsed', Date.now() - start));
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What are trade-offs between low vs high DNS TTL in this setup, and how would you monitor them?
- How would you validate TLS termination consistency across regions without changing apps?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to diagnose production latency where security tooling (TLS inspection) interacts with edge caches and rate limits.

## Key Concepts

- TLS inspection overhead and queueing
- Firewall connection limits and burst behavior
- Edge CDN caching and TTLs
- Observability: edge logs, pcap, and curl timing data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple latency probe using fetch
async function probe(url){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(url);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  console.log('latency', t1 - t0);
}
probe('https://edge.example/login');
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify bypass granularity while maintaining security?
- What metrics would you monitor during a peak event to alert on this issue?
